Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0800
 Subject: Patching kernel rk35xx files arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-yjh-jm10.dts

The MaskROM Type-C port (usbdrd_dwc3_0 / OTG0) currently runs in OTG
mode and is not used as a USB host on the JM10. Force it to
peripheral-only so the built-in g_serial gadget (CONFIG_USB_G_SERIAL=y,
set by the board hook) can expose a CDC-ACM serial console on ttyGS0.
Combined with "console=ttyGS0,115200" in extraargs, kernel logs can be
read from a host as /dev/ttyACM0 even though the board has no TTL
debug UART. The printk backlog is replayed when the gadget connects.

MaskROM and U-Boot RockUSB recovery through the same port are not
affected (they run at ROM/loader level, before Linux).

Signed-off-by: John Doe <john.doe@somewhere.on.planet>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-yjh-jm10.dts | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-yjh-jm10.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-yjh-jm10.dts
index 03f85444404e..e7a1b2c3d4e5 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-yjh-jm10.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-yjh-jm10.dts
@@ -1087,7 +1087,10 @@
 &usbdrd_dwc3_0 {
 	status = "okay";
 	extcon = <&u2phy0>;
-	dr_mode = "otg";
+	/* peripheral-only: expose this OTG port (the MaskROM Type-C) as a
+	 * CDC-ACM serial console (g_serial, ttyGS0) for debugging.
+	 * MaskROM/RockUSB recovery is unaffected (ROM level). */
+	dr_mode = "peripheral";
 };
 
 &u2phy0 {

